The idea is to split array into smaller components, sort them then merge them.
Worst case time is O(n Lg(n)). Lg n is the split part n being the merge part.

The operative idea being:
-> sorting smaller arrays are faster
-> merging sorted arrays is O(n) not O(n^2) (like it is with insertion sort)

=================================================
	RECURSIVE
=================================================
void mergesort(A, low, high) {
     if (low >= high) return;

     mid = (low + high) / 2;
     mergesort(A, low, mid);
     mergesort(A, mid + 1, high);
     merge(A, low, mid, high);
}

void merge(A, low, mid, high) {
     left  = low;
     right = mid + 1;
     size  = high - low + 1;

     for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {
     	 if (A[left] < A[right]) {
	    new[i] = A[left++];
	 } else if (A[left] > A[right]) {
	    new[i] = A[right++];
	 } else {
	    new[i] = A[left++];
	    right;
	 }
     }     
}

